# Imgcli in a Remotion project

- Discover current names with `npx @imgcli/cli list` or https://imgcli.com/llms-components.txt. Read the chosen component's Markdown page and installed interface.
- Install from the project root with `npx @imgcli/cli add <name>`. A project with `src/` receives `src/components/imgcli/`; otherwise files land in `components/imgcli/`. Imports are relative. No shadcn initialization or API key is required for free components.
- Scenes generally own their background; use their actual `theme`, `mode` and color props. Input and Caret are primitives with different APIs. Do not invent a shared `text` prop or a `speed` prop on primitives.
- Use local Sequence frames and budget from the current scene's default preview, then adjust for actual content and fps. The current catalog has standalone wipe scenes; arbitrary scene transitions use Remotion's own composition API.
- Replace sample media and claims with the user's real inputs. For unsupported capabilities such as word captions or a terminal recording, use an available tool or small project-local component rather than inventing registry names.
- Type-check, inspect stills across every beat and render the encoded video before claiming completion.
